       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nAs written, 2400 mg four times daily comes to **9,600 mg/day**. That is three times the maximum ibuprofen dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. A dose that high risks GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **600 mg PO four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day total.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day total.\n\nTypical dosing is 400\u2013800 mg per dose every 6\u20138 hours, with a maximum of 3,200 mg/day. Use the lowest effective dose for the shortest time, and give it with food.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. Please also confirm with your resident or attending. If 2400 mg per dose really was the intent, I'd want that verified with them before anything is ordered."
      }
